claim.claim-text:
a mandrel bladder (144);
a bladder vent aperture (146) formed in the mandrel bladder (144);
a mandrel vent aperture (150) in fluid communication with the bladder vent aperture (146); and
a vent fitting (148) that is configured to extend through the mandrel vent aperture (150) and to be coupled to the bladder vent aperture (146) such that the mandrel bladder (144) is in fluid communication with atmosphere that is external to the mandrel (104).

a vacuum channel (158) comprises
the mandrel vacuum channel (108) formed in the tooling surface (106); and
a second mandrel vacuum channel (128) formed in the tooling surface (106) and spaced away from the mandrel vacuum channel (108);

the mandrel vacuum channel (108) and the second mandrel vacuum channel (128) are located between the pair of seal grooves (136) formed in the tooling surface (106);
the mandrel (104) further comprises an inflatable seal (142) located between the mandrel vacuum channel (108) and the second mandrel vacuum channel (128); and
the inflatable seal (142) is configured to be pressurized to apply a force against the edge portion (116) of the vacuum-bag assembly (202) when the vacuum is being applied to the mandrel vacuum channel (108) and the second mandrel vacuum channel (128).

the tooling surface (106) is configured such that a perimeter vacuum chamber (206) is formed by the tooling surface (106), a bagging surface (168) of the vacuum-bag assembly (202), and the mandrel vacuum channel (108);
the mandrel (104) is configured such that the vacuum is applied to the perimeter vacuum chamber (206) via the mandrel vacuum channel (108) to form the vacuum seal (190);
the perimeter vacuum chamber (206) forms a portion of a perimeter boundary of the sealed vacuum chamber (184); and
the sealed vacuum chamber (184) is fluidly isolated from the perimeter vacuum chamber (206).
